---
// GitHub Pages serves `/404.html` for anything it cannot find, and only a file
// at that exact path. A page in the docs collection would build to `/404/`
// instead and never be reached, so this one lives in `src/pages/` -- which is
// the only thing in this site that does.
import StarlightPage from "@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro";
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: "That page is not here",
    template: "splash",
    pagefind: false,
  }}
>
  <p>
    It may have moved while this site was being written, or the link that
    brought you here may be older than the page it points at.
  </p>

  <p>Four places to look, which is the whole site:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/active_sanction/tutorial/"><strong>Get started</strong></a> —
      screening a name for the first time
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/active_sanction/how-to/"><strong>Guides</strong></a> — a
      specific job, for someone who already knows the domain
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/active_sanction/reference/"><strong>Reference</strong></a> —
      sources, configuration, errors, accuracy, the bundle format
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/active_sanction/explanation/"><strong>Explanation</strong></a> —
      how matching works, and why the defaults are what they are
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Generated API documentation is at
    <a href="/active_sanction/api/"><strong>/api/</strong></a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    If a link on this site brought you here, that is a bug in the site rather
    than a mistake you made. Please
    <a href="https://github.com/Babystep-Technologies/active_sanction/issues/new"
      >open an issue</a
    > and say which page you came from.
  </p>
</StarlightPage>
